      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T11:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  The check of whether the caller is CarrierConfig app has been done before this check when a network request with subID is received.\n\nDo you mean `enforceNetworkRequestPermissions`?\nI see `enforceNetworkRequestPermissions` is called only for Request type and `ensureSufficientPermissionsForRequest` is called for all network request including non-Request type.  \n\nI\u0027m not sure what is the purpose of this check.\n@benedictwong@google.com I saw this check was originally added by aosp/1652974.  \nDo you remember why we need this check?\nI\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s ok to skip this check always.",
      "parentUuid": "4bed927d_c04e0caf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7466,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 7466,
        "endChar": 42
