      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T11:16:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the `mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled` is true, enforceNetworkFactoryPermission is always skipped still.\n\nBased on the comment from Benedict, does the following make sense?\n```\nbool skipNetworkFactoryPermissionForRequest(nc) {\n  If (nc.getSubscriptionIds().isEmpty()) {\n      return true;\n  }\n\n  If (mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled \n        \u0026\u0026 canBypassRestrictedNetworkPermissionCheck) {\n     return true;\n  }\n  \n  return PermissionUtils.checkAnyPermissionOf(mContext,\n                android.Manifest.permission.CONNECTIVITY_USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS);\n   \n}\n\n\nif (!skipNetworkFactoryPermissionForRequest) {\n   enforceNetworkFactoryPermission();\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "14494369_a5b33407",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7466,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 7466,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
