      "writtenOn": "2024-01-24T04:14:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a possibility that `mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled` in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator is different from the one in ConnectivityService.\nCan we pass mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled from ConnectivityService?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24f21bec_ab93332e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-25T16:51:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator and ConnectivityService are from the same flag defined in ConnectivityFlags.java, how could the values be different? We can not pass the flag from ConnectivityService to CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator since ConnectivityService depends on CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator, but we can do it the othe way around, defining a getter method in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator so that ConnectivityService can get the flag from CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator, but frankly speaking I don\u0027t think that is a better way. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "4bb0cb77_8fdc9cd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c587d386_45e7e38e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T11:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`isFeatureEnabled` [read the flag value from DeviceConfig](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java;l\u003d211\n) and flag value is updated by flag push from server.\nSo If the flag value is updated between the two `isFeatureEnabled` calls, mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled value could be different.  \nI think this should be very rare but I felt it\u0027s safe to call `isFeatureEnabled` only once for REQUEST_RESTRICTED_WIFI flag.\nI thought we can pass flag from the constructor of `CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator`",
      "parentUuid": "24f21bec_ab93332e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6cb19750_8cbf6ceb",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T20:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Driveby comments, I\u0027ll trust Motomu\u0027s insight as the owner more than mine:\n\nI suspect that\u0027s impossible in practice; both of these are created exclusively at system server startup, prior to even system app startup (including GMS, which would write the deviceconfig flags). That said, there is a theoretical race.\n\nFrom an architectural standpoint, churning the constructor seems less than ideal, I\u0027d suggest maybe merging this into ConnectivityFlags, and passing that around as a central source of truth.",
      "parentUuid": "c587d386_45e7e38e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7d58bb3_bbbe94c6",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-27T01:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also feel that it is not a good idea to add the flag into the constructor, especially because we will need to remove it later. I am not sure whether moving those logic into ConnectivityFlags is a good idea either since there is no existing logic like that, so doing that means we need to copy part of the ConnectivityService#Dependencies logic into ConnectivityFlags.\n\n@motomuman@google.com which one do you prefer?\n1. Keep 2 flags as they are now\n2. Add the flag into the constructor of CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator\n3. Do the similar things as ConnectivityService#Dependencies in ConnectivityFlags",
      "parentUuid": "6cb19750_8cbf6ceb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12c45640_21086f97",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T11:16:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that reading flag value twice should not be the issue with the current flag update/rollback logic.  \nBut I still prefer not to depend on how the flag is updated or rollbacked currently and in the future.  \n\nCan we move all the flag check to ConnectivityService?  \nCurrent usage of mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator is callback handling and isCarrierServiceUidForNetworkCapabilities.\nFor callback handling, If ConnectivityService register the callback only when mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled is true, I think this check is enough.\n\nFor isCarrierServiceUidForNetworkCapabilities, I think ConnectivityService can pass mRequestRestrictedWifiEnabled as an argument.\n\n-----\nIf you don\u0027t like above proposal, I think we can do what Ying proposed on earlier comment (ConnectivityService call CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator method to check if the feature is enabled or not) or we can pass flag into the CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator constructor.\n\nFor ConnectivityFlags, I think we will need some work to use this for our use case and currently ConnectivityFlags is used to read only the single flag not used to read flags in general.\nSo I prefer the other options.",
      "parentUuid": "e7d58bb3_bbbe94c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "92c671c3b9c309edca6082a5142f7178fb0192fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
