    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80e10638_a11c73d3",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T11:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I read the design again and understand what you mean.\n\nBefore your CL, isCarrierServiceUidForNetworkCapabilities can not return true for WiFi networkRequest but could return true for Cellular network request.\nThis is because transportInfo is not requestable but network specifier is requstable.\n\nYou added `networkCapabilities.getSubscriptionIds().size() \u003d\u003d 1` to support WiFi network request.\nBut this work for cell network request as well.\n\nIs this understanding correct?\nCould you add comment to explain why we are getting subId from multiple places.\n\n-----\nI think subId we use could change for some cases by your change.\nbefore your CL, subId comes from from networkSpecifier or TransportInfo\nafter your CL, subId could come from networkCapabilities if the size of nc.subIds is 1.\nIs it safe? If it\u0027s safe can we always use nc.getSubscriptionIds()?\nI saw the wtf log at L298 and I\u0027m wondering.",
      "parentUuid": "a68501f8_8408b53a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 240,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 246,
